=\"result-number\">03</span>\n            <div class=\"result-page\"><strong>Colour swatches</strong><code>week3/ex3.html</code></div>\n            <span class=\"result-before\">84</span><span class=\"result-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span><span class=\"result-after\">100</span>\n            <span class=\"result-state\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">✓</span> Improved</span>\n          </article>\n          <article class=\"result-row\">\n            <span class=\"result-number\">04</span>\n            <div class=\"result-page\"><strong>CSS exercise page</strong><code>week3/ex8.html</code></div>\n            <span class=\"result-before\">92</span><span class=\"result-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span><span class=\"result-after\">100</span>\n            <span class=\"result-state\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">✓</span> Improved</span>\n          </article>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"results-caption\"><span class=\"caption-mark\" aria-hidden=\"true\">i</span> The report records four example scores. The other eight pages had the same title issue; the Week 2 pages were fixed the same way.</p>\n      </section>\n\n      <section class=\"report-section findings-section\" id=\"findings\" aria-labelledby=\"findings-title\">\n        <div class=\"section-heading\">\n          <div>\n            <p class=\"eyebrow\">02 — THE WORK</p>\n            <h2 id=\"findings-title\">Seven fixes, one clearer experience.</h2>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"section-aside\">The specific changes behind the score improvements.</p>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <section class=\"method-card\" id=\"method\" aria-labelledby=\"method-title\">\n        <div class=\"method-mark\" aria-hidden=\"true\">↗</div>\n        <div>\n          <p class=\"eyebrow\">03 — METHOD</p>\n          <h2 id=\"method-title\">Checked with Lighthouse.</h2>\n          <p>I ran the Lighthouse Accessibility audit in Chrome DevTools on the pages, addressed the reported issues, and ran the audi